  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0263df275083eba45b37ab9636c8dcbf, type: 3}
  m_Name: MAP-067_Frozen_Strait
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  mapId: MAP-067
  displayName: Frozen Strait
  environment: Arctic
  warfareFocus: Naval + Air + Ice Operations
  executiveSummary: Frozen Strait is a hybrid Arctic naval battlefield built for naval warfare, air operations, ice-field maneuvering, and autonomous multi-domain coordination. The terrain features fractured sea ice, narrow straits, iceberg clusters, frozen channels, coastal cliffs, submarine vents, and forward Arctic stations. The map emphasizes autonomous naval routing, air-sea coordination, sensor fusion under Arctic interference, and logistics under unstable ice conditions.
  designGoals:
  - name: Naval Warfare in Ice-Choked Waters
    description: Ship-to-ship combat, torpedo lanes, ice-breaker routes, and hull-hazard navigation. Ice floes create dynamic cover and movement obstacles.
  - name: Air Operations and Reconnaissance
    description: VTOL aircraft, drones, and long-range recon planes operate above the strait. Airspace corridors between cliffs and icebergs define movement and targeting.
  - name: Ice-Field Maneuvering
    description: Ground units traverse frozen channels, ice ridges, and unstable floes. Heavy armor risks breaking ice; light units excel in mobility.
  - name: Autonomy and Multi-Domain Coordination
    description: Autonomous units coordinate naval, air, and ice-field forces simultaneously. Units adapt to shifting ice patterns, fog pockets, and sonar interference.
  - name: Sensor and Information Warfare
    description: Sea fog, ice mist, thermal distortion, sonar scatter, and magnetic interference degrade sensors. Relay towers on cliffs restore clarity. Destroying relays creates blind pockets across the strait.
  - name: Logistics and Resources
    description: Fuel caches, coastal stations, and submarine vents serve as resupply nodes. Convoys must navigate ice-breaker routes and avoid ambush-prone channels.
  - name: Deployment and Progress
    description: A fixed deployment budget of approximately 10000 points forces players to choose between naval dominance, air superiority, or ice-field mobility. Blue deploys from the southwest coastal station; Red deploys from the northeast cliffside command.
  deployment: 'Deployment budget: approximately 10000 points. Blue deployment: southwest coastal station with naval staging. Red deployment: northeast cliffside command spire with AA emplacements. Neutral forward zone: outpost at (500,950) for drone resupply.'
  ar:
    viewingDistance: 4-5 m
    physicalArea: 10x10 m
    representedArea: Approximately 1 km2
    scale: 1:100
    fov: 53 degrees diagonal
    resolution: 1920x1080 per eye
    tracking: Inside-out horizontal-plane tracking; depth mesh if available
    interaction: Phone pointer for pan and zoom; HUD as screen-space widgets
  coordinateSystem: 1000x1000 grid; approximately 1 unit = 1 m. Origin (0,0) is the southwest corner.
  keyLocations:
  - name: Blue HQ - Coastal Station Bravo
    coordinate: (0,0)
    sizeOrElevation: 150x150 m
    description: Docks, fuel tanks, drone pads, and Arctic staging.
  - name: Red HQ - Cliffside Command Spire
    coordinate: (1000,1000)
    sizeOrElevation: 150x150 m
    description: Heated bunker with radar mast, AA emplacements, and sonar arrays.
  - name: Central Frozen Strait
    coordinate: (500,450)
    sizeOrElevation: 350x250 m
    description: Fractured ice, open-water lanes, iceberg clusters, and the naval combat zone.
  - name: Submarine Vent Field
    coordinate: (250,800)
    sizeOrElevation: 120x120 m
    description: Thermal vents, sonar distortion, and underwater hazards.
  - name: Ice Ridge Network
    coordinate: (800,300)
    sizeOrElevation: 200x200 m
    description: Wind-carved ridges, frozen tunnels, and flanking routes.
  - name: Ice-Breaker Channel
    coordinate: (0,450) to (400,900)
    sizeOrElevation: Primary naval chokepoint
    description: Narrow, hazardous channel that is constantly shifting.
  - name: Frozen Shore Route
    coordinate: (300,0) to (450,350)
    sizeOrElevation: Ground route
    description: Safer ground route with partial cover.
  - name: Cliff Relay A
    coordinate: (650,150)
    sizeOrElevation: +240 m
    description: Long-range sensor vantage point; approximately 350 m sensor coverage.
  - name: Cliff Relay B
    coordinate: (150,650)
    sizeOrElevation: +260 m
    description: Communications relay hub and sonar control node.
  - name: Neutral Forward Outpost
    coordinate: (500,950)
    sizeOrElevation: Forward resupply zone
    description: Drone resupply zone.
  chokepointsAndSightlines:
  - name: Ice-Breaker Channel
    description: Major naval chokepoint; controlling it determines sea movement.
  - name: Submarine Vent Field
    description: Thermal distortion disrupts sonar; ideal for submarine ambushes.
  - name: Frozen Strait Center
    description: Long-range naval and air engagements with dynamic ice cover.
  - name: Ice Ridge Network
    description: Interior flanking routes with unpredictable cover due to drifting snow and ice.
  - name: Sightlines
    description: Cliff Relay A provides approximately 350 m long-range sensor coverage. Sea fog and ice mist create fog-of-war pockets.
  terrain: Ice floes, frozen channels, cliffs, submarine vents, and coastal stations.
  vegetation: None; Arctic maritime zone.
  buildingsAndProps: 'Military: AA guns, radar dishes, sonar arrays, bunkers. Industrial: generators, pipelines, docks. Logistics: ships, cargo crates, fuel drums, and drones.'
  effects: Sea fog, ice mist, snowstorms, thermal distortion, and wave spray.
  audio: Wind, cracking ice, ship engines, sonar pings, and radio chatter.
  lodBudget:
  - category: Ice/Terrain
    count: 3
    trianglesPerItem: 200000
    totalTriangles: 600000
  - category: Naval/Industrial
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 80000
    totalTriangles: 320000
  - category: Buildings/Military
    count: 15
    trianglesPerItem: 50000
    totalTriangles: 750000
  - category: Roads/Paths
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 30000
    totalTriangles: 120000
  - category: Props
    count: 50
    trianglesPerItem: 10000
    totalTriangles: 500000
  textureBudget: 2048x2048 for terrain and buildings; 1024x1024 for props. DXT1/5 compression. Target 100 MB or less.
  engineAndPlugins: 'Source specification: Unreal ARTemplate and Nreal SDK (XREAL); ARKit/ARCore enabled. This project is being added to the existing Unity map database; engine integration requires separate compatibility review.'
  rendering: Forward renderer, stationary lights, baked global illumination, and aggressive culling (source specification).
  anchors: Single spatial anchor for the entire map.
  interaction: Phone pointer for pan and zoom; HUD as screen-space widgets.
  multiplayer: Client-server architecture; offload AI and physics to server.
  milestones:
  - name: Month 1 - Prototype Layout
    description: Block out the strait, ice ridges, submarine vents, and test the AR anchor.
  - name: Month 2 - Core Systems
    description: Implement navigation meshes for ice and land, naval autonomy, and air-sea coordination.
  - name: Month 3 - AR Integration
    description: Implement anchors, plane detection, and basic interactivity.
  - name: Months 4-5 - Content Fill
    description: Create final models, textures, lighting, and audio.
  - name: Months 6-7 - Gameplay and Polish
    description: Implement objectives, balancing, and visual effects for sea fog, ice mist, and thermal distortion.
  - name: Month 8 - Testing and QA
    description: Multiplayer stress testing and sensor validation.
  testing:
  - name: Autonomy
    description: Verify naval routing, air-sea coordination, and ice-field navigation.
  - name: Communications and Sensors
    description: Test relay destruction, fog-of-war updates, and sonar interference.
  - name: Performance
    description: Target at least 60 Hz AR rendering on the target device.
  - name: QA Checklist
    description: Test navigation, naval logic, deployment budget enforcement, anchor drift, and sensor accuracy.
